# Statistics Simulation Lab

A collection of Python simulations designed to build intuition for probability, randomness, sampling, and statistical inference.

Each module explores a statistical question through simulation and visualization.

## Completed Modules

* Coin Flip Simulation
* Dice Simulation
* Sampling Distribution Simulation
* Central Limit Theorem Simulation

## Project Goals

This project is intended to strengthen my understanding of introductory statistics while developing practical Python programming skills.

The simulations focus on connecting statistical theory with computational experiments by generating random data, analyzing results, and creating visualizations.

## Planned Modules

* Confidence Interval Simulation
* Hypothesis Testing Simulation
* Regression Basics
* Monte Carlo Simulation
* Law of large numbers
* Variance and standard deviation
